% Your code goes here
syms s K
L = K*(s+1)/(s^4+(29/2)*s^3+(134/2)*s^2+(185/2)*s);
Kv = limit(s*L, s, 0);
K_staticError = Kv %[output:05619b86]
%[text]  What is the steady state error of the closed loop system in response to a unit step input? Assign your answer the variable $\\texttt{e\\\_stepQ3a}$
% Type 0: NO integrator in L(s)
syms s K
L = K*(s+1)/(s^4+(29/2)*s^3+(134/2)*s^2+(185/2)*s);

% Position constant
Kp = limit(L, s, 0);           % just evaluate at s=0

% Steady state errors
K_staticErrorPosition = Kp             % step input %[output:440879e4]
e_stepQ3a=1/(1+K_staticErrorPosition) %[output:142b06d4]
%[text]  What is the steady state error of the closed loop system in response to a unit ramp input? Assign your answer the variable $\\texttt{e\\\_rampQ3a}$
% Your code goes here
e_rampQ3a=1/K_staticError %[output:29bb3fb7]
%[text] c) (10 marks) For $G(s)=\\frac{s+1}{s^4+\\frac{29}{2}\\,s^3+\\frac{134}{2}\\,s^2+\\frac{185}{2}\\,s}$ design a controller more complex controller $D(s)$ so that the closed loop system is stable and tracks ramps with zero steady state error. Pick a gain value $K$for your controller so that the closed loop system visibly converges to ramp input when you simulate the first 5-10 seconds of a ramp input to the system.
